MID_SC30_00_m01: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m01_001: What?! The White-Maned Demon—here?!
MID_SC30_00_m01_002: I demand an explanation. How did you come to be\nking of Brezarant?
MID_SC30_00_m01_003: Let's catch up later, shall we, Queen of Saramis?\nThere's a battle for us to win.
MID_SC30_00_m01_004: I wish I understood what is happening here. But you\nare correct that it can wait.
MID_SC30_00_m20: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m01_005: Strike now, while our enemy is reeling! Do not give\nthem an opportunity to regroup!
MID_SC30_00_m01_006: All troops, forward, and wipe out any foe before you!
MID_SC30_00_m02: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m02_001: Withdraw, Cai, or risk bringing grief to your mother.
MID_SC30_00_m02_002: I'm sorry, Theodora, but I can't do that.
MID_SC30_00_m03: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m03_001: What are you doing here? Go away. Get back to\nyour family!
MID_SC30_00_m03_002: I'm sorry, Leda. How did it come to this?
MID_SC30_00_m04: 
MID_SC30_00_m04_001: 
MID_SC30_00_m04_002: 
MID_SC30_00_m05: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m05_001: Cai, we don't have to do this! Let's go back to the\nvillage together!
MID_SC30_00_m05_002: I'm sorry, Peter, but someone has to look out for Pop.
MID_SC30_00_m06: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m06_001: Cai, you have to retreat! I can't fight you!
MID_SC30_00_m06_002: I'm sorry, Ultand, for any mistakes that led me here.
MID_SC30_00_m07: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m07_001: I don't want war, but this is the only way for me to\nsave Pop.
MID_SC30_00_m08: 
MID_SC30_00_m08_001: 
MID_SC30_00_m08_002: 
MID_SC30_00_m09: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m09_001: Leda, what are you doing here?!
MID_SC30_00_m09_002: Step aside, Cai. You've had a happy childhood—\nyou would never understand my motivations.
MID_SC30_00_m10: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m10_001: Look around, Bertrand. This is the place where\nyou die!
MID_SC30_00_m11: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m11_001: Miss Leda...is this really what you want?
MID_SC30_00_m11_002: Shut up and have at me, Sirocco, before I burn you to\na crisp.
MID_SC30_00_m12: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m12_001: Leda, please don't do this! I don't want to fight you.
MID_SC30_00_m12_002: Then why are you standing in the way of my\nvengeance?
MID_SC30_00_m13: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m13_001: It's your lucky day, Olympia! We can finally settle\nthis ridiculous feud.
MID_SC30_00_m13_002: Leilidahna, this isn't the ending I had in mind.
MID_SC30_00_m14: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m14_001: I'll sacrifice anything—everything!—if it means\nhe dies.
MID_SC30_00_m15: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m15_001: If you're looking for a worthy foe, look no further.\nThe Catoblepas, Nathan Bakaudi, has arrived!
MID_SC30_00_m16: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m16_001: I am Creek Avancio, the Pantere, and I have come\nto claim your life.
MID_SC30_00_m17: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m17_001: This is absurd! How could they have pressed the\nattack this far?!
MID_SC30_00_m18: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m18_001: Traitors to the Dagdan Empire... Your corpses will\nbe mounted as a warning to all who defy us!
MID_SC30_00_m19: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_m19_001: They've left us no choice but to retreat and regroup\nat Agris Stronghold.
MID_SC30_00_m19_002: Enjoy your fleeting victory, insurgents. I'll be settling\nthe score with you later.
MID_SC30_00_e01: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_e00_001: The enemy general has fallen! Let us dispose of\nhis dregs.
MID_SC30_00_e02: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_e02_001: If I can make a name for myself in this fight, then\nmaybe I can rescue my dad.
MID_SC30_00_e02_002: Theodora... I'm really sorry, but this is the only\nchoice I have left.
MID_SC30_00_e03: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_e03_001: I absolutely will not retreat. For Cai's sake.
MID_SC30_00_e04: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_e04_001: I drifted here in search of a place to die...and now I\nmeet you! Of all people!
MID_SC30_00_e04_002: It's over, Bertrand. I'm ending you!
MID_SC30_00_e05: <TH>
MID_SC30_00_e05_001: I will accompany milady until the bitter end.
MID_SC30_01_m01: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m01_001: Do not be intimidated by the fortress's reputation.\nIn the end, it is a bastion like any other.
MID_SC30_01_m01_002: Keep one eye on the enemy's defensive forces,\nand press the attack with vigor!
MID_SC30_01_m02: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m02_001: On my honor, no traitor against the empire will pass!
MID_SC30_01_m03: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m03_001: I find myself grateful to your army. This battle is\nmore thrilling than any I've ever fought!
MID_SC30_01_m04: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m04_001: Well? Why have you not struck the killing blow?
MID_SC30_01_m04_002: Heh. This is the last place I had expected such\na show of mercy.
MID_SC30_01_m04_003: In all honesty...I owe the lot of you a debt.
MID_SC30_01_m04_004: And so it shall be repaid. I, Creek Avancio, am at\nyour army's service.
MID_SC30_01_m05: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m05_001: No one...no one has ever dared to assault Agris\nStronghold in the history of our empire.
MID_SC30_01_m05_002: Come on, Ianuarius! Get a hold of yourself!
MID_SC30_01_m05_003: Now is my chance to show I'm equal to such a dismal\nsituation. This is my time to shine!
MID_SC30_01_m06: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m06_001: Agris Stronghold is mine. And I won't let you\nwretches take it from me.
MID_SC30_01_m07: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m07_001: Very well then, the fortress is yours. You've forced\nmy hand.
MID_SC30_01_m07_002: But don't confuse victory here with winning the war.\nSavor these small triumphs while you can...
MID_SC30_01_m08: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_m07_003: That's...disquieting. What do you think he meant?
MID_SC30_01_e02: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_e02_001: General Lind has withdrawn! Make Lieutenant\nIanuarius your next priority!
MID_SC30_01_e03: <TH>
MID_SC30_01_e03_001: We have dispatched Lieutenant Ianuarius.\nBut let us not rest until General Lind falls!
MID_SC30_03_m01: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m01_001: I finally return to Grand Aragon...and I'm here to\nattack it. Strange.
MID_SC30_03_m01_002: But I'm not here for revenge—it's for justice that I\nturn my blade against my homeland.
MID_SC30_03_m16: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m01_003: Queen Aswan, look. The Alliance!
MID_SC30_03_m01_004: There are soldiers stationed everywhere defending\nthe capital. We must move carefully.
MID_SC30_03_m01_005: Evade capture, and reach the Alliance as soon\nas we can.
MID_SC30_03_m02: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m02_001: Is my king still alive and well? Good, then I'm not\ntoo late.
MID_SC30_03_m02_002: How could that man have sped here from the front\nlines in so short a time?
MID_SC30_03_m02_003: Yes, well done, Nathan. Now, protect me.\nProtect me, I say!
MID_SC30_03_m03: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m03_001: Died like a dog. Useless! You were supposed to keep\nme safe!
MID_SC30_03_m04: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m04_001: Aswan! What are you doing out here?
MID_SC30_03_m04_002: I want to help!
MID_SC30_03_m04_003: You mean...join the battle against your own country?\nAre you certain?
MID_SC30_03_m04_004: Yes. I am firm in my decision.
MID_SC30_03_m04_005: Very well, Aswan. But promise me you will survive.
MID_SC30_03_m05: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m05_001: You there! You're in the Alliance, right? Let me\nhelp you!
MID_SC30_03_m05_002: Aswan? You're the queen. What are you doing here?
MID_SC30_03_m05_003: Leda! Oh, I'm so glad to see you. I've long been\nwishing I could thank you.
MID_SC30_03_m05_004: I don't need your thanks. I just followed my heart.
MID_SC30_03_m05_005: But it is comforting, having you with us.
MID_SC30_03_m06: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m06_001: I am Aswan Hasdrubal Aragon, queen of the\nkingdom of Arago.
MID_SC30_03_m06_002: Please, allow me to help you!
MID_SC30_03_m07: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m07_001: Creek?! I don't believe this. What the hell are\nyou thinking?!
MID_SC30_03_m07_002: So sorry, old friend. This sort of thing happens in\nwar sometimes.
MID_SC30_03_m08: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m08_001: Hear me, Alliance! I will lay down my life to keep\nyou from trampling on my country's soil!
MID_SC30_03_m09: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m09_001: That wound I gave you isn't lethal. I'm being sincere\nfor once when I say you should join me, Nathan.
MID_SC30_03_m09_002: I'd rather die than live on in disgrace like you!
MID_SC30_03_m09_003: Listen to me. Dagda the Great, and his lackey\nKing Gilchris...they fight for nothing.
MID_SC30_03_m09_004: Rather than offer these tyrants our blind loyalty,\nwouldn't it be better to follow our hearts?
MID_SC30_03_m09_005: Ah?!
MID_SC30_03_m10: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m10_001: Bertrand, come to destroy the object of your hatred.
MID_SC30_03_m10_002: That's why you're here, isn't it? Your heart yearns for\nvengeance!
MID_SC30_03_m10_003: No, Gilchris.
MID_SC30_03_m11: 
MID_SC30_03_m11_001: 
MID_SC30_03_m11_002: 
MID_SC30_03_m12: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m12_001: King Gilchris... As frightening as you are, I cannot\nafford to run away.
MID_SC30_03_m12_002: What a cruel injustice, that I must face in battle\nFatima's spitting image!
MID_SC30_03_m12_003: Fatima? Ah! What is this feeling...
MID_SC30_03_m13: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m13_001: Queen of Saramis, you she-devil. You should have\nsubmitted quietly to your destruction!
MID_SC30_03_m13_002: Though I may die, I shall never submit. We will\nsurvive. And in the end, we will win.
MID_SC30_03_m14: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m14_001: I'm sorry, Gilchris. I cannot stand by as you destroy\nmy kingdom.
MID_SC30_03_m14_002: Aswan—you as well? So deep is your desire for\nBertrand, you would take up arms against me?!
MID_SC30_03_m14_003: Fine. What do I need you for anyway? Die, my\ntraitorous wife!
MID_SC30_03_m15: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_m15_001: Stand against Arago, and you pay the price in flesh!
MID_SC30_03_e01: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_e01_001: Curse you, bastards! I'll show you.
MID_SC30_03_e01_002: Now, set loose the flames! They will all burn,\nalong with this whole damn city!
MID_SC30_03_e02: <TH>
MID_SC30_03_e02_001: How could he... Gilchris, is this how far\nyou've fallen?
MID_SC30_05_m01: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m01_001: Advance, vanguard troops, and crush every last one\nof the rebels.
MID_SC30_05_m01_002: B-but there's too many of them! They'll punch right\nthrough our defenses!
MID_SC30_05_m01_003: Don't question me. Do it, or I'll have you flayed and\nimpaled for your insolence.
MID_SC30_05_m01_004: If you fear death so badly, then fight until there's\nno one left to kill you.
MID_SC30_05_m02: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m02_001: Hey there, Majesty. As lovely as it is to see you, I'm\nafraid I'll be stopping you here.
MID_SC30_05_m02_002: Yet I cannot afford to back down either. Anyone\nwho stands in my way must fall.
MID_SC30_05_m03: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m03_001: Talimun, are you really siding with them?
MID_SC30_05_m03_002: Stand down, boy, this is adult business! A child like\nyou could never understand.
MID_SC30_05_m04: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m04_001: Man, what a nightmare. Alright, if I have to kill such\na beautiful woman, let's just get it over with.
MID_SC30_05_m04_002: Oh, is Mr. Big-Shot Merchant gonna hold back?\nBecause I sure won't.
MID_SC30_05_m05: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m05_001: Damn it, Talimun, don't do this! We're supposed to\nbe a team. We're supposed to protect each other!
MID_SC30_05_m05_002: Calm down, Simon. Just be a pal and stay out of\nmy way.
MID_SC30_05_m06: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m06_001: Talimun... I...
MID_SC30_05_m06_002: Ohhh, what's the matter? Where's that usual\nLulu resolve?
MID_SC30_05_m07: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m07_001: Talimun, I beg of you! Please, let's just run\naway together!
MID_SC30_05_m07_002: Sorry, Fianna, but I have bigger plans than whatever\nyou and I would be.
MID_SC30_05_m08: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m08_001: Know this wasn't my first choice. But weighing my\ngoals against all of you... Well, try not to hate me.
MID_SC30_05_m09: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_m09_001: You may have backed me into a corner, but you'll\nfind that's when I'm at my most dangerous.
MID_SC30_05_m09_002: I told you damned rebels I'd settle with you.\nAnd now that time has come!
MID_SC30_05_e01: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_e01_001: Look. I know we've been through a lot together, but\nthis time is different. This will be life or death.
MID_SC30_05_e01_002: I'll show you what a difference the experience\nof age can make.
MID_SC30_05_e02: <TH>
MID_SC30_05_e02_001: If we survive this...I'll tell Talimun the truth...\nI'll tell him how I feel.
MID_SC30_06_m01: 
MID_SC30_06_m01_001: 
MID_SC30_06_m01_002: 
MID_SC30_06_m02: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m02_001: Sweetie, you... You're the one person I never wanted\nto have to fight.
MID_SC30_06_m02_002: But that's what you want, isn't it? So I'll do it.\nBecause I love you.
MID_SC30_06_m02_003: Yes, Esmeralda. That is what I ask of you. Show me\nwhat you are truly capable of.
MID_SC30_06_m03: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m03_001: There's no point in wasting my breath. Because this\nis all you want from me.
MID_SC30_06_m03_002: OK, so I will waste a little breath. I thought we had\ncome together.
MID_SC30_06_m03_003: I am sorry. But it is too late for me to change.
MID_SC30_06_m04: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m04_001: Come, let us dance the dance of damnation together!
MID_SC30_06_m05: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m05_001: I'll make you rue the day you defied me!
MID_SC30_06_m06: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m06_001: So he has shown his face after all. The circumstances\nhere prevent us from using the star again...
MID_SC30_06_m06_002: Aim for the godshield on his brow—a dragon's\nweak point!
MID_SC30_06_m06_003: Credna, you slime! You think you'll get away with\nthis rank betrayal?!
MID_SC30_06_m07: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m07_001: Ugh. It helps us little to know the weak point if it's\ncovered in impenetrable scales.
MID_SC30_06_m07_002: Stand firm! There must be some trick yet to play—\nsome other means of getting through it!
MID_SC30_06_m10: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m07_003: Hmm...
MID_SC30_06_m07_004: Who is THIS?!
MID_SC30_06_m07_005: You're the one in white who always helped us.
MID_SC30_06_m07_006: You! I know you.
MID_SC30_06_m07_007: You...are you the one in white who appeared before\nme through the years?
MID_SC30_06_m07_008: Of all the people to come help us... It's you!
MID_SC30_06_m07_009: 
MID_SC30_06_m07_010: 
MID_SC30_06_m07_011: 
MID_SC30_06_m07_012: We have arrived at the perfect moment. Fear not!\nI am here to provide the chance you hoped for!
MID_SC30_06_m09: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m09_001: Impossible... What power could pierce my defenses?\nWho the hell are you?
MID_SC30_06_m09_002: The attack exposed Father's godshield! Everyone,\ntake full advantage—now!
MID_SC30_06_m09_003: We must defeat him! He brings only tragedy after\ntragedy to the world!
MID_SC30_06_m08: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m08_001: This is the height of futility. The likes of you can't\ndo anything to me.
MID_SC30_06_m11: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_m08_002: Damned vermin... Don't think for one second that\nyou're better than me!
MID_SC30_06_e01: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_e01_001: You can't seriously think you've got me at a\ndisadvantage.
MID_SC30_06_e01_002: Never have mere humans inflicted such wounds\nagainst me, I'll grant you that.
MID_SC30_06_e01_003: But the tables are about to turn. All you've done is\nnothing more to me than the buzzing of a fly's wings!
MID_SC30_06_e03: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_e03_001: <DLG>{CapitalizeNextLetter}{AvatarName} vanished into thin air.
MID_SC30_06_e04: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_e04_001: Lyrah... I chose to stand by your side.
MID_SC30_06_e04_002: Show me what lies beyond this war. Show me the\nfuture that guides you.
MID_SC30_06_e05: <TH>
MID_SC30_06_e05_001: I shall accompany you. I find myself intrigued to\nuncover what it is that you seek.
MID_SC30_07_m01: <TH>
MID_SC30_07_m01_001: So you have come. Just know that your struggle\nis futile.
MID_SC30_07_m01_002: Your motives elude me, but I at least understand that\nwe are on the verge of an atrocity.
MID_SC30_07_m01_003: All forces, target the dragon! We must put a stop\nto her scheme!
MID_SC30_07_m02: <TH>
MID_SC30_07_m02_001: *sigh*
MID_SC30_07_m02_002: It's like some kind of...cocoon!
MID_SC30_07_m02_003: Whoa! Hey! What's happening?!
MID_SC30_07_m02_004: Lyrah... What is your plan?
MID_SC30_07_m02_005: I don't understand what that is...but I have a pretty\ngood idea what to do to it.
MID_SC30_07_m02_006: 
MID_SC30_07_m02_007: 
MID_SC30_07_m02_008: Do not relent! That thing must be destroyed!
MID_SC30_07_m03: <TH>
MID_SC30_07_m03_001: You are too late. Soon, the underworld will be born.
MID_SC30_07_m04: <TH>
MID_SC30_07_m04_001: Ah...
MID_SC30_08_m01: <TH>
MID_SC30_08_m01_001: We gotta get outta here.
MID_SC30_08_m01_002: The desire to enter the gate tugs at me...but no. We\nmust retreat for now.
MID_SC30_08_m01_003: There will be no victory here. Everyone, retreat as\nquickly as you are able!
MID_SC30_08_m01_004: Well, that's that. We're done here! Time to run?
MID_SC30_08_m01_005: 
MID_SC30_08_m01_006: 
MID_SC30_08_m01_007: 
MID_SC30_08_e01: <TH>
MID_SC30_08_e01_001: I mislike the look of the warriors in the center.\nGive them a wide berth.